In the case of Nd, all terms of the index (m*TILE_WIDTH+ty)*Width + Col have the same value for all threads in the same warp except for the tx term in Col. Note that all threads in the same warp have adjacent tx values; therefore, adjacent threads in a warp access adjacent elements in a row. The hardware detects that these threads in the same warp access consecutive location in the global memory and combine them into a coalesced access.

